rc-plc/pennsylvania/fayette-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, August to September has come in under 90% of normal in 34 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids, more than any other pair since 1951. In 2025 that same pair ran 61% of normal on the middle, and April to May ran 151%. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 54% on the middle. Grid 24201 had its driest year in 1963 at 71% and has been under 90% in 20 years.</p>"}
